    "durationMs": 206044,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app: `models.py` (SQLAlchemy `Link` model), `schemas.py` (pydantic validation: absolute http/https URL with host, code charset `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), `routers/links.py` (all four endpoints), `main.py` (exception handlers mapping every error to `{\"error\": ...}` JSON)\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — migration `0001` creates the `links` table (unique indexed code, 2048-char url, clicks, created_at)\n- `start.sh` — applies `alembic upgrade head` then `exec uvicorn` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; works from any cwd\n- `README.md`, `requirements.txt` (pinned, no extras needed), `tests/` (30 tests)\n\n**Key behaviors verified over real HTTP**\n- `POST /links` returns 201 with the submitted URL unchanged (query/fragment preserved); duplicate custom code → 409; generated codes are 8-char, unique via IntegrityError retry\n- `GET /r/{code}` returns 302 with exact `Location` and uses an atomic SQL `clicks = clicks + 1` — verified incrementing exactly once per request\n- Malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL, invalid codes (including in paths) all → 422 with `error` field; unknown codes → 404\n- **Persistence across restart**: created a link, clicked it, killed the server, restarted — clicks and data survived; `alembic upgrade head` is a no-op on the second run\n\nOne environment quirk I handled: `DATABASE_URL` uses the `postgresql://` scheme, but SQLAlchemy needs the psycopg 3 dialect, so `app/config.py` rewrites it to `postgresql+psycopg://` at load time.\n\nFinal state: 30/30 tests pass, test data truncated for a clean handoff, no servers left running."
